    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0731" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114A/219</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-05T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 5, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 7, 4.41
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5057. For War Trade Board [from Dresel]:</p>
                <p>No. 205. Inter-Ally Commission of Berne has refused all applications, principally
                    originating with Y.M.C.A. here, to send to Russian prisoners in Germany articles
                    of any nature, including such as are used for religious services. I concur fully
                    but at instance of Doctor Harte I request
                    definite ruling from you on subject. Dresel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
